{"parentUuid":"b8c1d560-6f4b-46f5-b183-31dc0c42f40d","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a89d19953587dd79f","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Wx7md3qTVSZAg19CdD8ujQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HV4vxbPbMpbiMoB47A3CHc","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"cpsat-autotune d-krupke Optuna OR-Tools CP-SAT parameter tuning github"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8022,"cache_read_input_tokens":13113,"output_tokens":269,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8022},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":269,"cache_read_input_tokens":13113,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8022,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8022,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caot1GmRFAV57kR1Qo3rj","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"f0aa89be-8bc5-4350-bbf6-f8ee1ac1fb5e","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:59:21.069Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"b8c1d560-6f4b-46f5-b183-31dc0c42f40d","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"a89d19953587dd79f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01T1ixoNSmBuUT8hRcKgsD6Q","type":"tool_result","content":"# cpsat-autotune Project Summary\n\n## Project Description\nA Python library for optimizing hyperparameters of Google's OR-Tools CP-SAT solver for specific problem instances, leveraging the Optuna optimization framework.\n\n## Current Version & Release Info\n- **Latest Version:** 0.6.0 (uses parameters from CPMPy as default)\n- **Last Commit:** 49 commits on main branch\n- **Star Count:** 25 stars\n\n## Dependencies\nThe documentation references:\n- **Optuna** - for hyperparameter optimization\n- **Google OR-Tools** - specifically the CP-SAT solver\n- **CPMPy** - parameters sourced from this library (v0.6.0+)\n\nSpecific version numbers for Optuna and OR-Tools aren't listed in the provided content.\n\n## Main API Entry Points\n1. `tune_time_to_optimal()` - minimizes time to find optimal solutions\n2. `tune_for_quality_within_timelimit()` - maximizes/minimizes objective value within time constraints\n3. `import_model()` - loads models from protobuf files\n4. CLI commands: `time`, `quality`, `gap`\n\n## Supported Tuning Methods\n- Time-to-optimal minimization\n- Quality optimization within time limits\n- Gap minimization for complex models\n\n## README Quickstart Example\n```python\nfrom cpsat_autotune import import_model, tune_time_to_optimal\nmodel = import_model(\"models/medium_hg.pb\")\nbest = tune_time_to_optimal(model, max_time_in_seconds=3, n_trials=50)\n```\n\n## File/Module Structure\n- `/src/cpsat_autotune/` - main source code\n- `/tests/` - test suite\n- `/models/` - example model files\n- `.github/workflows/` - CI/CD configuration\n- Example notebooks: `example.ipynb`, `example_packing.ipynb`\n\n**License:** MIT"}]},"uuid":"f35474b3-1eb1-4800-8c66-6749165bd526","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:59:26.989Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b8c1d560-6f4b-46f5-b183-31dc0c42f40d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"f0aa89be-8bc5-4350-bbf6-f8ee1ac1fb5e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"a89d19953587dd79f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HV4vxbPbMpbiMoB47A3CHc","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"cpsat-autotune d-krupke Optuna OR-Tools CP-SAT parameter tuning github\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-autotune: WIP: Tune the hyperparameters of Google's OR-Tools' CP-SAT solver for specific models · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-autotune\"},{\"title\":\"cpsat-autotune · PyPI\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/cpsat-autotune/0.2.0/\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding the Log - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/understanding_the_log.html\"},{\"title\":\"Basic Modeling - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/04_modelling.html\"},{\"title\":\"Dominik Krupke - The CP-SAT Primer\",\"url\":\"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/dominik-krupke-9869b2241_github-d-krupkecpsat-primer-using-and-activity-7178425582915829760-y-D2\"},{\"title\":\"Coding Patterns - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/06_coding_patterns.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-logutils: Utils for parsing the logs of OR-Tools' CP-SAT solver.\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-logutils\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about cpsat-autotune:\n\n## Overview\n\ncpsat-autotune is a Python library designed to optimize the hyperparameters of Google's OR-Tools CP-SAT solver for specific problem instances. cpsat-autotune uses the optuna library to perform hyperparameter tuning on a preselected set of parameters.\n\n## Key Features\n\nWhile CP-SAT is already highly optimized for a broad range of generic problems, fine-tuning its parameters for particular problem sets can yield significant performance gains. This tool leverages the optuna optimization library to systematically explore and suggest optimal hyperparameter configurations tailored to your needs.\n\nThe output of optuna is then further refined and the significance of certain parameters is evaluated.\n\n## Use Cases and Limitations\n\nIt is specifically designed to enhance solver efficiency in targeted scenarios, particularly within the context of Adaptive Large Neighborhood Search (ALNS). However, cpsat-autotune is not a universal solution that guarantees a performance boost for all uses of the CP-SAT solver.\n\n## Related Resources\n\nThe search results also revealed related projects by the same author (d-krupke):\n- The CP-SAT Primer: A comprehensive guide to Google's OR-Tools CP-SAT solver.\n- CP-SAT Log Analyzer: A tool to analyze the logs generated by Google's OR-Tools CP-SAT solver.\n\nThe GitHub repository for cpsat-autotune is available at: https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-autotune\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"c41781b5-11ac-492f-812c-f25883b7b870","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:59:27.913Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f0aa89be-8bc5-4350-bbf6-f8ee1ac1fb5e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
