{"parentUuid":"27d36722-2b50-46f6-a6c9-37e1c8127536","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a89d19953587dd79f","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_011YKpKeCfsNTmJFPw5TCUed","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LRLaY94XWMKeqNuUF5m97V","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-autotune/tree/main/src/cpsat_autotune","prompt":"List every file in this directory and describe its purpose. I want to understand the module structure: which file holds the parameter search space, which holds the Optuna objective wrapper, which holds tuning entry points."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2384,"cache_read_input_tokens":21135,"output_tokens":375,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2384},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":375,"cache_read_input_tokens":21135,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2384,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2384,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caot2CiN1PZrBTn7Ck4xZ","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"b39fea8f-d8ec-4383-8105-8857ec90c340","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:59:33.729Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"b39fea8f-d8ec-4383-8105-8857ec90c340","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"a89d19953587dd79f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LRLaY94XWMKeqNuUF5m97V","type":"tool_result","content":"# cpsat-autotune Module Structure\n\nBased on the directory listing, here are the key files and their purposes:\n\n**Parameter Space & Configuration:**\n- **`parameter_space.py`** - Defines the search space for hyperparameter tuning\n- **`cpsat_parameters.py`** - Contains CP-SAT specific parameter definitions\n- **`parameters.py`** - General parameter handling and management\n\n**Optimization & Evaluation:**\n- **`parameter_evaluator.py`** - Evaluates parameter configurations during search\n- **`objective.py`** - Wraps the optimization objective (likely for Optuna framework)\n- **`tune.py`** - Primary tuning orchestration and entry point\n\n**Supporting Infrastructure:**\n- **`caching_solver.py`** - Implements solver caching to avoid redundant computations\n- **`model_loading.py`** - Handles loading optimization models\n- **`model_filter.py`** - Filters or preprocesses models\n- **`metrics.py`** - Defines performance metrics for evaluation\n- **`print_result.py`** - Formats and displays tuning results\n\n**CLI & Execution:**\n- **`cli.py`** - Command-line interface for the tuning tool\n- **`__main__.py`** - Entry point for running as a module\n- **`__init__.py`** - Package initialization\n\nThe core workflow flows through `tune.py` (orchestration), `objective.py` (optimization target), and `parameter_space.py` (search domain)."}]},"uuid":"258a11fe-43ce-4a29-840b-b73c4d5fa60a","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:59:38.068Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b39fea8f-d8ec-4383-8105-8857ec90c340","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"27d36722-2b50-46f6-a6c9-37e1c8127536","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"a89d19953587dd79f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01T4fGjH8Abt8oyQDaokZ3KG","type":"tool_result","content":"# cpsat-autotune: Key Technical Details\n\n## Core Functionality\n\n**cpsat-autotune** is a Python library that optimizes Google OR-Tools CP-SAT solver hyperparameters using the Optuna optimization framework. The tool focuses on improving performance for problem instances solved repeatedly with time constraints, particularly in Adaptive Large Neighborhood Search contexts.\n\n## Installation & Basic Usage\n\nInstallation via pip:\n```bash\npip install -U cpsat-autotune\n```\n\nModel import and tuning example:\n```python\nfrom cpsat_autotune import import_model, tune_time_to_optimal\n\nmodel = import_model(\"models/medium_hg.pb\")\nbest = tune_time_to_optimal(\n    model,\n    max_time_in_seconds=3,\n    n_samples_for_trial=5,\n    n_samples_for_verification=20,\n    n_trials=50,\n)\n```\n\n## Tuning Methods\n\n### tune_time_to_optimal\nMinimizes time to find optimal solutions. Parameters include:\n- `model`: CP-SAT model\n- `max_time_in_seconds`: solve time limit\n- `relative_gap_limit`: optimality gap (default: 0.0)\n- `n_samples_for_trial`: samples per trial (default: 10)\n- `n_samples_for_verification`: verification samples (default: 30)\n- `n_trials`: trial count (default: 100)\n\n### tune_for_quality_within_timelimit\nMaximizes/minimizes objective value within time constraints. Accepts the same parameters plus `obj_for_timeout` and `direction` ('maximize'/'minimize').\n\n## Tuned Parameters Example\n\nFrom the documented output, optimized parameters included:\n- `cp_model_probing_level`: Set to 0 (default: 2)\n- `cut_level`: Set to 0 (default: 1)\n\nThese showed reported improvements from mean 1.61 seconds (default) to 0.48 seconds (optimized) across 20 verification samples on the tested model.\n\n## CLI Commands\n\n**time command:**\n```sh\ncpsat-autotune time --max-time 60 --relative-gap 0.01 --n-trials 50 \n  --n-samples-trial 5 --n-samples-verification 20 path/to/model/file\n```\n\n**quality command:**\n```sh\ncpsat-autotune quality --max-time 60 --obj-for-timeout 100 --direction maximize \n  --n-trials 50 --n-samples-trial 5 --n-samples-verification 20 path/to/model/file\n```\n\n**gap command:**\nMinimizes optimality gap within time limits (useful for complex models unlikely to reach optimality).\n\n## Important Limitations\n\nThe documentation emphasizes that results \"should be considered as a suggestion for further evaluation rather than definitive settings\" due to sampling methodology. Key challenges include CP-SAT's high variance across random seeds, the large hyperparameter space, and difficulty determining statistical significance of parameter changes versus default well-tuned settings."}]},"uuid":"914fe828-b19a-4689-8ba6-8f3e15ab53da","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:59:40.573Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"27d36722-2b50-46f6-a6c9-37e1c8127536","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"914fe828-b19a-4689-8ba6-8f3e15ab53da","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a89d19953587dd79f","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01JEnGfLXMabMjTZVnvNWZub","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Tkddq5766rD3cPKCFm4qwJ","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/d-krupke/cpsat-autotune/main/src/cpsat_autotune/parameter_space.py","prompt":"List every CP-SAT parameter that this file defines as part of the search space. For each, show the type (categorical/int/float), the values/range, and any default. Show the exact code structure and any Optuna trial.suggest_* calls."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":525,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1408,"cache_read_input_tokens":23519,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1408,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":73,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011Caot38wvbtCphED6Drueu","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"4f44570c-b570-4b34-913e-e03f82c87533","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:59:44.709Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"4f44570c-b570-4b34-913e-e03f82c87533","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a89d19953587dd79f","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01JEnGfLXMabMjTZVnvNWZub","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MkNNZiQMWRQimA5PyDweq4","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/d-krupke/cpsat-autotune/main/src/cpsat_autotune/objective.py","prompt":"Show how the Optuna objective is defined. Specifically: how does it run CP-SAT, how does it handle multiple samples per trial, does it support parallel trials, does it handle timeouts/crashes, does it support warmstarts/checkpoints, and what does it return to Optuna."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":525,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1408,"cache_read_input_tokens":23519,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1408,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":73,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011Caot38wvbtCphED6Drueu","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"b7f01541-516e-4675-b335-fc5457f5d15c","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:59:47.044Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"4f44570c-b570-4b34-913e-e03f82c87533","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"a89d19953587dd79f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Tkddq5766rD3cPKCFm4qwJ","type":"tool_result","content":"# CP-SAT Parameters in Search Space\n\nThis file does **not define** the actual parameters themselves. Instead, it manages a parameter space imported from elsewhere.\n\nThe code references:\n- `CPSAT_PARAMETERS` - imported from `.cpsat_parameters`\n- This is a list of parameter objects with these interface methods:\n  - `param.name` - parameter identifier\n  - `param.sample(trial)` - generates values via Optuna\n  - `param.get_cpsat_default()` - CP-SAT default value\n  - `param.is_effective_for(model)` - applicability check\n  - `param.get_optuna_default()` - Optuna default value\n\n## Parameter Details\n\nThe actual parameter definitions (types, ranges, defaults, and `suggest_*` calls) reside in the `cpsat_parameters.py` module, which is **not included** in the provided content.\n\nThe `CpSatParameterSpace` class acts as a wrapper that:\n- Filters parameters by applicability to models\n- Samples parameters through Optuna trials\n- Converts between Optuna and CP-SAT value formats\n- Returns non-default values only\n\nTo list the specific CP-SAT parameters, you would need to examine the `cpsat_parameters.py` file."}]},"uuid":"a0c25e69-a4d9-435b-b93b-9a20566b668b","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:59:48.684Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4f44570c-b570-4b34-913e-e03f82c87533","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"a0c25e69-a4d9-435b-b93b-9a20566b668b","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a89d19953587dd79f","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01JEnGfLXMabMjTZVnvNWZub","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BhvTq4cByW2eNwK8KsvQtB","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/d-krupke/cpsat-autotune/main/src/cpsat_autotune/tune.py","prompt":"Show the public API: tune_time_to_optimal, tune_for_quality_within_timelimit, and any other entry points. Show how Optuna study is configured (sampler choice — TPE/CMA-ES/Random, n_jobs for parallelism, storage backend for checkpointing, pruners). Show how baseline default params are evaluated for comparison."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":525,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1408,"cache_read_input_tokens":23519,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1408,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":73,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011Caot38wvbtCphED6Drueu","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"e654f59c-a85d-4ee4-9ee0-c63493c620ce","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:59:49.080Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"b7f01541-516e-4675-b335-fc5457f5d15c","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"a89d19953587dd79f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MkNNZiQMWRQimA5PyDweq4","type":"tool_result","content":"# Optuna Objective Definition in OptunaCpSatStrategy\n\n## CP-SAT Execution\nThe objective runs CP-SAT indirectly through the `scorer.evaluate()` method, which wraps model solving. The actual CP-SAT invocation is abstracted away in the `CachingScorer` class.\n\n## Multiple Samples Per Trial\nThe strategy uses a two-phase approach:\n1. **Initial phase**: Evaluates with `n_samples_for_trial` runs (default: 10)\n2. **Verification phase**: If results are competitive, re-evaluates with `n_samples_for_verification` runs (default: 30)\n\nThis adaptive sampling increases confidence in promising solutions.\n\n## Parallel Trial Support\nThe code does not explicitly address parallelization. The `CachingScorer` suggests potential caching mechanisms, but nothing in this implementation prevents or enables parallel trial execution.\n\n## Timeout/Crash Handling\nNo timeout or crash handling is visible. The `knockout_score` parameter appears to short-circuit unpromising trials early, but no exception handling or recovery mechanisms are implemented.\n\n## Warmstart/Checkpoint Support\nThe code provides `best_params()` to retrieve optimal parameters found so far, but no serialization, checkpoint saving, or warmstart initialization is present.\n\n## Return Value\nThe objective returns `score.mean()` to Optuna—a single float representing the mean performance across multiple samples, enabling Optuna to guide its search algorithm."}]},"uuid":"d16f1d63-25fe-4961-94bd-4f208f923da6","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:59:51.365Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b7f01541-516e-4675-b335-fc5457f5d15c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"e654f59c-a85d-4ee4-9ee0-c63493c620ce","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"a89d19953587dd79f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BhvTq4cByW2eNwK8KsvQtB","type":"tool_result","content":"# CP-SAT Hyperparameter Tuning API\n\n## Public Entry Points\n\nThe library exposes three main tuning functions:\n\n1. **`tune_time_to_optimal()`** – Minimizes time to find an optimal solution\n2. **`tune_for_quality_within_timelimit()`** – Maximizes/minimizes objective value under time constraints\n3. **`tune_for_gap_within_timelimit()`** – Minimizes optimality gap within time limits\n\nAll return optimized parameter dictionaries.\n\n## Optuna Study Configuration\n\nThe study is initialized with minimal configuration:\n\n```python\nstudy = optuna.create_study(\n    direction=objective.scorer.metric.direction,\n    sampler=optuna.samplers.TPESampler(),\n)\n```\n\n**Key observations:**\n- **Sampler**: TPE (Tree-structured Parzen Estimator) is hardcoded—no alternative sampler options\n- **Parallelism**: Not configured; no `n_jobs` parameter visible\n- **Storage/Checkpointing**: No persistent backend specified; study exists only in memory\n- **Pruning**: No pruner is defined\n\n## Baseline Evaluation\n\nDefault parameters are evaluated before optimization:\n\n```python\ndefault_baseline = scorer.evaluate({}, n_samples_for_verification)\n```\n\nThe baseline uses empty parameters `{}` (triggering defaults) and is measured across `n_samples_for_verification` runs. Results display min/mean/max statistics and serve as comparison when printing final results via `print_results()`."}]},"uuid":"88e97158-df72-4004-94ec-3a26031d3984","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:59:53.803Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e654f59c-a85d-4ee4-9ee0-c63493c620ce","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
