{"parentUuid":"ccc9ae22-4d54-456c-ab57-e70303927964","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"a89d19953587dd79f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018W5CsE5DtzMjAqwpGxt89m","type":"tool_result","content":"REDIRECT DETECTED: The URL redirects to a different host.\n\nOriginal URL: https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-autotune/raw/main/example.ipynb\nRedirect URL: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/d-krupke/cpsat-autotune/main/example.ipynb\nStatus: 302 Found\n\nTo complete your request, I need to fetch content from the redirected URL. Please use WebFetch again with these parameters:\n- url: \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/d-krupke/cpsat-autotune/main/example.ipynb\"\n- prompt: \"Find any mentions of speedup percentages, baseline timing vs tuned timing, the model name being tuned, and concrete numeric results. Also any mention of \"70%\" speedup.\""}]},"uuid":"956fbc31-b799-41d5-9112-c1cd263c43a2","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:00:14.066Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ccc9ae22-4d54-456c-ab57-e70303927964","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"3b3b62e8-bc65-414b-b4dd-36a4c84de019","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"a89d19953587dd79f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NsV8k4ifyfdgYfiZ9AXBu3","type":"tool_result","content":"# CachingScorer Analysis\n\n## Caching Strategy\nThe caching scorer caches by **parameters only**, not by model or seed. It creates cache keys using `frozenset` of parameter pairs, converting lists/tuples to sorted tuples for consistency. The cache is an in-memory dictionary (`dict[frozenset, MultiResult]`) with no disk persistence mechanism visible in this code.\n\n## Solver Execution\nThe scorer runs CP-SAT through `cp_model.CpSolver()`, configuring it by:\n- Setting parameters directly on `solver.parameters`\n- Creating `SatParameters()` objects for subsolver-specific parameters\n- Applying both variable parameters and fixed parameters via `setattr()` and `extend()` methods\n\nThe metric is invoked as `self.metric(solver, self.model)`, suggesting the metric itself handles the actual solve call.\n\n## Randomness Handling\nThe code provides **no explicit seed management**. When running multiple samples (`num_runs`), it simply executes `n_missing` iterations without varying seeds. Randomness across samples would depend on CP-SAT's internal default behavior or any randomization the metric implementation applies.\n\n## Key Limitation\n\"Computing the score for a given set of parameters involves running the solver multiple times. As this can be computationally expensive, the results are cached to avoid redundant computations.\" However, **no disk persistence is implemented**—the cache exists only during runtime."}]},"uuid":"9f3dc605-a145-4afe-b181-bd0069dd235a","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:00:17.482Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3b3b62e8-bc65-414b-b4dd-36a4c84de019","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
